      "message": "Ugh... I can\u0027t even reason about this (and the the empty `textual_headers` in the new `:hsw`). It would take me all day. If they\u0027re not in `textual_headers` then (at least in g3 with their weird module system) each of the headers will get pre-compiled the first time they are used. But there are rules about how they are compiled when cached which makes this difficult to reason about. I mean, the issue here is that we\u0027re building a separate version of Skia in general for a different architecture than what we\u0027re actually targeting, but we\u0027re shoving into the same binary as the Skia for the \"base\" architecture. (We\u0027re really creating a fat binary, but doing so ourselves to avoid being super fat.)",
